XHTML documents in Universal mode: a document starting with an XML
declaration whose first start tag declares the XHTML namespace follows XML
rules. Void elements without an end tag are closed before the next token.
-- Document universal --
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>x</title><script>a&amp;&lt;b</script><style><![CDATA[a<b]]></style></head><body><p>a<p>b</p></p><br><img src="x"/></body></html>
-- tokens --
0 ProcInst xml "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>" data=" version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\""
0 Text "\n" text="\n"
0 Doctype "<!DOCTYPE html>"
0 Text "\n" text="\n"
1 StartTag html "<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
2 StartTag head "<head>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 StartTag title "<title>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "x" text="x"
3 EndTag title "</title>"
3 StartTag script "<script>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "a&amp;&lt;b" text="a&<b"
3 EndTag script "</script>"
3 StartTag style "<style>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 CDATA "<![CDATA[a<b]]>" text="a<b"
3 EndTag style "</style>"
2 EndTag head "</head>"
2 StartTag body "<body>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "a" text="a"
4 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
4 Text "b" text="b"
4 EndTag p "</p>"
3 EndTag p "</p>"
3 StartTag br "<br>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 EndTag br [implied] ""
2 StartTag img [self-closing] "<img src=\"x\"/>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" src="x"
2 EndTag body "</body>"
1 EndTag html "</html>"
-- NoNamespace universal --
Without a namespace declaration, elements follow HTML rules.
-- in --
<html><head><title>x<b/></title></head><body><p>a<p>b</body></html>
-- tokens --
1 StartTag html "<html>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
2 StartTag head "<head>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 StartTag title "<title>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "x<b/>" text="x<b/>"
3 EndTag title "</title>"
2 EndTag head "</head>"
2 StartTag body "<body>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "a" text="a"
3 EndTag p [implied] ""
3 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
3 Text "b" text="b"
3 EndTag p [implied] ""
2 EndTag body "</body>"
1 EndTag html "</html>"
-- VoidElements universal --
Void elements under XML rules open an element. Their end tag closes it if it
comes next, and otherwise an implied end tag closes it before the next token,
which is then read without it. Self-closed ones don't open an element. After
the html element, the document still follows XML rules, and the br there is
in no namespace.
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="utf-8"></meta><link rel="x">
<title>t</title></head><body><p>a<br></br>b<br/>c<br>d<br><!--x--><br><i>e</i><br></p><hr><?pi x?><br><![CDATA[x]]><img src="y"></BR><input></body></html><br>
-- tokens --
